          {
            "name": "Tissue perfusion",
            "stage": "Raw data",
            "description": "Pass when tissue is sufficiently well-perfused and extracted to meet experimental needs. Good tissue perfusion will preserve gross anatomical structures without cracks in tissue, and will be free of perfusion-related artifacts. Sufficient tissue perfusion will meet experimental needs, but may have some tissue damage or broad-spectrum autofluorescent artifacts (e.g. bright, visible vasculature). Fail when tissue damage or artifacts render the sample unsuitable for meeting experimental needs.",
